Subject: [PATCH] Avoid stale QRhi access after widget recovery

After WindowAboutToChangeInternal releases a widget's resources and removes
its cleanup callback, the old QRhi pointer is retained until the next paint.
Recovery can destroy that QRhi while a hidden or idle widget still holds it.
Guard callback removal in repeated window changes and widget destruction
with the registration state introduced by patch 0069. Keep resource teardown
for widgets that own an offscreen QRhi without a registered callback.

This closes the G03, G05, G06 and G09 crash paths exposed by recovery retries
and device monitoring in patches 0070 and 0071.

diff --git a/src/widgets/kernel/qrhiwidget.cpp b/src/widgets/kernel/qrhiwidget.cpp
index a28f53e5c17..b4a6006a51c 100644
--- a/src/widgets/kernel/qrhiwidget.cpp
+++ b/src/widgets/kernel/qrhiwidget.cpp
@@ -211,7 +211,9 @@ QRhiWidget::~QRhiWidget()
     Q_D(QRhiWidget);
 
     if (d->rhi) {
-        d->rhi->removeCleanupCallback(this);
+        // An unregistered QRhi may have been destroyed since the last window change.
+        if (d->rhiCleanupRegistered)
+            d->rhi->removeCleanupCallback(this);
         // rhi resources must be destroyed here, due to how QWidget teardown works;
         // it should not be left to the private object's destruction.
         d->resetRenderTargetObjects();
@@ -295,7 +297,7 @@ bool QRhiWidget::event(QEvent *e)
         // returning the existing QRhiTexture in the meantime.
         d->textureInvalid = true;
 
-        if (d->rhi && d->rhi != d->offscreenRenderer.rhi()) {
+        if (d->rhi && d->rhiCleanupRegistered && d->rhi != d->offscreenRenderer.rhi()) {
             // Drop the cleanup callback registered to the toplevel's rhi and
             // do the early-release, there may not be another chance to do
             // this, and the QRhi we have currently set may be destroyed by the
